From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liu <7runv6se@duck.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:37:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(daemon): proxy-authenticated multi-user mode with local
 teams

Add OD_PROXY_AUTH=1 for self-hosted deployments behind an authenticating
reverse proxy (e.g. oauth2-proxy). The daemon trusts the proxy-asserted
email header and replaces the Vela workspace directory with a local
SQLite team store:

- collab/local-teams.ts: teams + members tables; every user gets a
  Personal workspace plus one directory entry per team membership.
- http/proxy-identity.ts: requires the email on non-loopback requests,
  strips client x-od-workspace-* headers and re-derives them from the
  local directory (403 for non-members); admin gate for shared settings.
- Project gate: in proxy mode unbound projects are denied and headerless
  requests are scoped to the project's workspace for the verified user.
- Workspace directory, members, team catalog and invites are served
  from the local store; /team-admin page manages teams and members.
- Memory is disabled in proxy mode (daemon-wide store would leak
  between users); OD_WORKSPACE_SETTINGS_URL points team management links
  at the local page.

Upstream behavior is unchanged when OD_PROXY_AUTH is unset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
